// Reviewer correction: switched from GroundAoe's `pooled_debuff` (instant,
// non-lingering) to `StaticAura` (see transmutation/plant_growth.ron), which
// leaves a real, reapplying zone behind at the caster's position for
// `aura_duration` -- a much closer match to "a bank of mist that billows
// out and lingers" than a one-shot burst. No vision-occlusion/concealment
// mechanic exists (checked common/src/comp/buff.rs in full); `Blinded`'s own
// doc comment explicitly calls this out ("vision occlusion is a deferred
// client-only effect") and is the closest already-shipped analog reused
// here rather than inventing a new BuffKind. `StaticAura` always places the
// zone at the caster's own position (no aimed placement exists,
// common/src/states/static_aura.rs) -- the sheet's 37 m cast range isn't
// mechanically expressed, the same simplification transmutation/
// plant_growth.ron and transmutation/control_winds_turbulence.ron already
// ship with.
StaticAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    energy_cost: 40.0,
    targets: OutOfGroup,
    auras: [
        (kind: Blinded, strength: 0.4, duration: Some(2), category: Some(Magical)),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(15.0),
    range: 6.0,
    sprite_info: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Primordial)),
)
